Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: pdphy: always return the RX buffer

qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy_pd_receive() bails out without writing
USB_PDPHY_RX_ACKNOWLEDGE when the reported size is invalid or a register
read fails. Software then keeps owning the RX buffer and the PHY stops
accepting, and therefore GoodCRC-ing, every following message until
set_pd_rx() runs again on a hard reset.

Seen on a OnePlus 7 Pro with powered USB-C docks: the dock's PS_RDY after an
Accept (and after a PR_SWAP) is never acknowledged (the dock's next message
reuses MessageID 2), pd_transmit_payload() reports "RX message pending", and
messages flow again only after each hard reset. The result is a hard-reset
loop and a dropped DisplayPort/USB session ~2.5 s after docking.

Hand the buffer back on every path once the RX IRQ has fired, and report
dropped frames instead of hiding them behind dev_dbg.
Nura-Category: upstream-fix
Nura-Origin: nura rc4d dock debugging
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2 (RX buffer leaked on error paths)
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c	2026-11-13 20:33:26.416626227 +0100
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c	2026-11-13 20:34:26.576453481 +0100
@@ -337,12 +337,13 @@
 	ret = regmap_read(pmic_typec_pdphy->regmap,
 			  pmic_typec_pdphy->base + USB_PDPHY_RX_SIZE_REG, &size);
 	if (ret)
-		goto done;
+		goto ack;
 
 	/* Hardware requires +1 of the real read value to be passed */
 	if (size < 1 || size > sizeof(msg.payload) + 1) {
-		dev_dbg(dev, "pd_receive: invalid size %d\n", size);
-		goto done;
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(dev, "pd_receive: invalid size %u, dropping\n", size);
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		goto ack;
 	}
 
 	size += 1;
@@ -351,19 +352,28 @@
 			  &rx_status);
 
 	if (ret)
-		goto done;
+		goto ack;
 
 	ret = regmap_bulk_read(pmic_typec_pdphy->regmap,
 			       pmic_typec_pdphy->base + USB_PDPHY_RX_BUFFER_REG,
 			       (u8 *)&msg, size);
 	if (ret)
-		goto done;
+		goto ack;
 
-	/* Return ownership of RX buffer to hardware */
-	ret = regmap_write(pmic_typec_pdphy->regmap,
-			   pmic_typec_pdphy->base + USB_PDPHY_RX_ACKNOWLEDGE_REG, 0);
+ack:
+	/*
+	 * Return ownership of the RX buffer to hardware on every path once the
+	 * IRQ has fired. While software owns it the PHY does not accept, and so
+	 * never GoodCRCs, the next message: a dropped frame here used to make
+	 * the following PS_RDY vanish and stall PD until the next hard reset.
+	 */
+	{
+		int ack_ret = regmap_write(pmic_typec_pdphy->regmap,
+					   pmic_typec_pdphy->base + USB_PDPHY_RX_ACKNOWLEDGE_REG, 0);
+		if (!ret)
+			ret = ack_ret;
+	}
 
-done:
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pmic_typec_pdphy->lock, flags);
 
 	if (!ret) {
